# Cloudflare Pages _headers — Phase X · X-7 / L-1, revised in CF-1.
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for the rationale per directive.
#
# STATUS: these headers become REAL on Cloudflare Pages. They were dead on
# GitHub Pages, which does not read this file — so for the whole life of this
# file every directive below was aspirational, and DEPLOYMENT.md's "contract"
# was fiction. That flips the moment the Cloudflare deploy is live, which is
# exactly why the COEP line had to go before it did (see below). CSP remains
# enforced via the <meta> tag in index.html; meta CSP cannot express
# frame-ancestors or report-uri (per W3C spec), so X-Frame-Options carries
# the framing defense.

/*
  # HSTS with preload. `.capital` is not a preloaded TLD (unlike .app/.dev),
  # so this is what earns twinsphinx.capital the same guarantee: a year-long
  # max-age plus subdomains, which is what hstspreload.org requires before it
  # will accept a manual submission. Submitting is a one-time human step —
  # see DEPLOYMENT.md. Until then this still protects every returning visitor.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  # Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
  # `require-corp` would block every cross-origin subresource that does not
  # opt in with CORP/CORS headers — including the Google Fonts stylesheet and
  # font files loaded from index.html WITHOUT a crossorigin attribute. On
  # GitHub Pages this line was inert so nobody noticed; on Cloudflare it would
  # have gone live and silently broken typography across the whole app on the
  # first deploy. Re-adding it requires adding crossorigin to those tags (and
  # verifying the fonts CDN sends CORP) first — do not restore it casually.
  # We gain nothing today by having it: COEP exists to unlock
  # crossOriginIsolated APIs (SharedArrayBuffer, high-res timers) and this app
  # uses none of them.
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
